### Search strategy (two-pass)

**Pass 1 — broad search:**
```
?search=TITLE&per_page=5&select=...
```
Decision logic:
- No results → return `{}`
- `top_score < MIN_SCORE_FLOOR (40)` → return `{}`
- `top_score >= MIN_SCORE_ABSOLUTE (1000)` AND `title_overlap >= 0.30` → accept
- `top_score >= MIN_SCORE_ABSOLUTE (1000)` AND `title_overlap < 0.30` → return `{}`
- `gap < SMALL_GAP_THRESH (0.60)` → go to Pass 2
- `gap >= 0.60` AND `overlap >= 0.30` → accept
- `gap >= 0.60` AND `overlap < 0.30` → return `{}`

Title overlap = `len(query_words ∩ result_title_words) / len(query_words)`

**Pass 2 — strict title filter + soft author check:**
```
?filter=title.search:TITLE&per_page=5&select=...
```
- No results → return `{}`
- Has results:
  - Extract surnames from `authors` list (last word of each name)
  - Check if any surname appears in any author's display_name (case-insensitive)
  - Surname match found → accept top result
  - No surname match AND gap > 0.80 → accept top result (soft gate)
  - No surname match AND gap <= 0.80 → return `{}`

**IMPORTANT: Do NOT append author surnames to the `?search=` query.** Testing showed this destroys scores (13060 → 171 for "Attention is all you need Vaswani"). Author matching is client-side only.

### Calibrated thresholds (from empirical testing)
```python
MIN_SCORE_FLOOR       = 40      # below this = no match
MIN_SCORE_ABSOLUTE    = 1000    # above this = immediate accept (with overlap check)
SMALL_GAP_THRESH      = 0.60    # gap between rank1 and rank2 scores
TITLE_OVERLAP_THRESH  = 0.30    # word overlap between query and result title
PASS2_SOFT_GAP        = 0.80    # accept without author match if gap this large
```

### Rate limiting
Stub worker currently sleeps 1-3s between requests. Tighten to 0.5-1.0s — OpenAlex polite pool allows ~10 req/s.

