## Empirically calibrated search thresholds

From test runs against real papers in the collection:

| Query type | Score range | Gap | Decision |
|---|---|---|---|
| Exact title match | 1149–13060 | >186% | ACCEPT absolute |
| Truncated title (line break) | 1230 | >1340% | ACCEPT absolute |
| OCR cleaned old paper | 39.91 | 383% | REJECT (below floor=40) |
| Wrong author appended | 4.57 | 345% | REJECT (below floor) |
| Generic chemistry title | 1559 | 13% | RETRY pass2 |
| Ambiguous short title | 3076 | 223% | ACCEPT absolute |
| OCR garbage | no results | — | return {} |

**Critical insight:** Do NOT append author surnames to `?search=` query. "Attention is all you need" scores 13060. "Attention is all you need Vaswani" scores 171 (rank 1 is a wrong paper). Author matching must be client-side only, in Pass 2 using `filter=title.search:`.

